-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",78,{
[2465]="700662B1\n1\tDolvir has asked you to convince war-weary Corsairs to seek him out for help. You can find weary Corsairs in Abadec's Watch in the south-west corner of Belfalas.\t\n2\tTalk to Dolvir outside Abadec's Watch\tYou have successfully convinced many weary Corsairs to leave Abadec's Watch. Dolvir waits for you amongst the trees to the north of the camp. You should talk to him.\n",
[2466]="7005B18A\n1\tDestroy Orkish provisions at Kamaz-kala\tOrkish provisions can be found at Kamaz-kala at Azanulbizar. You should destroy Orkish provisions at Kamaz-kala.\n2\tDestroy Orkish provisions at Kamaz-kala (total: 8)\tOrkish provisions can be found at Kamaz-kala at Azanulbizar. You should destroy Orkish provisions at Kamaz-kala.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many Orkish provisions at Kamaz-kala.\n",
[2467]="700082EA\n1\tDefeat Natkam\tThe goblin-taskmaster Natkam patrols the goblin-camps on the outskirts of the Orc-host in Dol Dínen. You should sever the thread that holds the goblins together: defeat Natkam, who leads them.\n2\tDefeat Natkam\tThe goblin-taskmaster Natkam patrols the goblin-camps on the outskirts of the Orc-host in Dol Dínen. You should sever the thread that holds the goblins together: defeat Natkam, who leads them.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Natkam, the leader of the goblins. Their forces will scatter without his brutal will forced upon them.\n",
[2468]="70027181\n1\tAssist Melvun at the Barnavon Mine\030Assist Argel at the Barnavon Mine\030Assist Bervun at the Barnavon Mine\030Assist Cada at the Barnavon Mine\tThe Barnavon Mine lies far to the east of Barnavon-town, beyond the tower of Hen Turrau. Gwilum has asked you to lend aid to the miners at the Barnavon Mine so that Madin Brenin will not punish the Boar-clan for the disruption of ore production.\n2\tMelvun is at the Barnavon Mine, east of Barnavon. Gwilum is at Barnavon, west of the Barnavon Mine. You should speak with either Melvun or Gwilum regarding your successes at the Barnavon Mine.\t\n",
[2469]="7004178B\n1\tTalk to Faltharan\tFaltharan is located at the steps to Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Faltharan.\n",
[2470]="7004956E\n1\tAid Spakorth in learning the fates of his brethren in the Oath-taker's Horn\030Aid Gimli in freeing the Stout-axes who refuse to follow King Greytooth\030Aid Gimli in hindering the Firehorn smiths\tGimli and Spakorth can be found along the causeway outside the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth. Gimli and Spakorth have asked you to aid them in hindering the Firehorns in their quest to recover the lost Dwarf-ring, Manthríf.\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the Oath-taker's Horn\tGimli might be found in the heights of the Oath-taker's Horn. You have done much to hinder the Stout-axes loyal to King Greytooth and aid those who have defied him. You should now seek Gimli in the Oath-taker's Horn.\n",
[2471]="70046C20\n1\tDestroy bear-traps along the road through Cirith Negen (total: 10)\tBear-traps can be found along the road through Cirith Negen in north-eastern North Ithilien. Anborn has asked you to investigate reports that the path through Cirith Negen is being readied for a Khundolar ambush. You should disarm traps and defeat any foes you encounter.\n2\tTalk to Tordoron to the north of Cirith Negen\tTordoron can be found to the north of Cirith Negen. You have disarmed the traps and fought off Khundolar trapping the pass of Cirith Negen. You should now seek out Tordoron beyond the pass.\n",
[2472]="700357C4\n1\tDefeat Isengard overseers (total: 2)\030Defeat Orcs at Drû Vádokan (total: 8)\tDrû Vádokan can be found in north-west Balewood. Barallas wants you to return to the White Hand camp and thin their numbers while the Ents travel closer to the camp.\n2\tTalk to Barallas outside Drû Vádokan\tBarallas can be found nearby outside Drû Vádokan. You have thinned the ranks of the White Hand in the Balewood and should now return to Barallas and prepare for their final assault against the Orc forces.\n",
[2473]="700272B2\n1\tDestroy crates of black fire (total: 5)\tCrates of black fire can be found within Uvel-cadlus. Thurbald has asked you to enter Uvel-cadlus and destroy the Draig-lûth's supply of black fire.\n2\tTalk to Thurbald\tThurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus. You should return to Thurbald with news of your success.\n",
[2474]="70001202\n1\tDefeat Orc-warriors (total: 4)\030Defeat Orc-defilers (total: 3)\030Defeat Orc-skirmishers (total: 4)\tThere are Blogmal and Krahjarn Orcs throughout Eastern Malenhad, north of Gabilshathûr. Gisur has asked you to defeat many Orcs in an attempt to give the dwarves of Gabilshathûr some breathing-room.\n2\tTalk to Guard-captain Gisur\tGuard-captain Gisur is at Gabilshathûr, south of Duvuinen. You have defeated a large number of Orcs and should return to Gisur to inform him of your success.\n",
[2475]="700381C2\n1\tDefeat the Shakh-hai Overseers ([see journal]/3)\tThree of Sarumans most feared Shakh-hai warriors have launched a surprise assault on the right flank of the wall. This trio of Shakh-hai overseers possess abilities that will strengthen the morale of their troops, while crushing and humiliting the champions of Helm's Deep in front of their own troops, broadly demoralizing them, unless the Shakh-hai can be stopped - and quickly. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2476]="7000C0A6\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance to the Men of Bree.\n",
[2477]="7000C0A7\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Men of Bree.\n",
[2478]="7000C0A8\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Men of Bree.\n",
[2479]="7000C0A9\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Men of Bree.\n",
[2480]="7000AC69\n1\tBring the Bree-spear to Maggie Smallwood\030Collect a Bree-spear\tMaggie Smallwood is at the Bree Hunting Lodge, west of the South-gate. Maggie Smallwood has requested that you bring her a crafted Bree-spear to help the woodworkers of Bree arm the Watchers.\n",
[2481]="70000CE9\n1\tTalk to Guardsman Otley\tTrestlebridge is to the north, along the route called the Greenway. Speak to Guardsman Otley in Trestlebridge and learn how you can help with the town's defence.\n",
[2482]="70050A16\n1\tDestroy drake eggs (total: 12)\tYou should destroy any drake eggs that you find on the Withered Heath.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed many drake eggs.\n",
[2483]="7004D091\n1\tTalk to Fotri\tYou should speak with Fotri, who can be found in Forochel.\n2\tTalk to Fotri\tYou should speak with Fotri, who can be found in Forochel.\n",
[2484]="70021CB1\n1\tDefeat Heilun Brenin's personal guards (total: 3)\030Defeat Heilun Brenin\tHeilun Brenin and his guards can be found at the centre of Gwâl Draig, east of Gronu's camp. Gronu asked you to defeat Heilun Brenin and his personal guards.\n2\tTalk to Gronu at his camp\tGronu's camp lies to the west of Gwâl Draig, beneath Harndirion. You should seek out the Gronu and inform him that Heilun Brenin and his men have been defeated.\n",
[2485]="7004BEB8\n1\tDefeat Khirgi's Bridge Guards (total: 4)\tKhirgi's Bridge Guards can be found in Fushaum Bal North. You should defeat the men guarding the bridge to Fushaum Bal North.\n2\tTalk to Mâlatuk\tMâlatuk can be found at Fushaum Bal South. You should talk to Mâlatuk.\n",
[2486]="7001AA6D\n1\tDefeat brigands and half-orcs in Andrath (total: 20)\tHalf-orcs and brigands can be found in the ruins of Andrath. Watcher Brittleleaf is enraged by the actions of the brigands and half-orcs holding the ruins of the Southwatch and wants you to strike a decisive blow against them.\n2\tTalk to Watcher Brittleleaf\tWatcher Brittleleaf and Watcher Oakdale can be found hidden to the east of the northern end of the ruins. You brought justice to the fiends in the ruins of Southwatch and should return to Watcher Brittleleaf.\n",
[2487]="70065787\n1\tDiscover Hata Kebir\tBrigands have flooded the recently abandoned Hata Kebir.\n2\tDefeat brigands in Hata Kebir (total: 12)\tBrigands have flooded the recently abandoned Hata Kebir, east of Aerthir. Defeat brigands.\n3\tTalk to Aerin\tTell Aerin that you have defeated brigands at Hata Kebir.\n",
[2488]="70066280\n1\tDiscover the Bolt-holes\tBrigands are hiding out in the Bolt-holes.\n2\tDefeat brigands (total: 10)\tBrigands are hiding out in the Bolt-holes. Defeat brigands.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many brigands in the Bolt-holes.\n",
[2489]="700375CD\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tReeve Fríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should bring Captain Grimmar's recommendation to Reeve Fríthild.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tReeve Fríthild is at her encampment to the south of Stoke, just off the road on the other side of the bridge on the road to Kingstead. Reeve Fríthild asked you to meet her at her encampment.\n3\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild at her camp\tReeve Fríthild is at her encampment to the south of Stoke. You should speak with Reeve Fríthild regarding the battle.\n4\tThe Reeve of Stoke is in the Mead Hall. The Reeve instructed you to meet in Stoke to plan for the next attack.\t\n",
[2490]="7001482B\n1\tScout dead-end passages (total: 3)\030Scout intact passages (quantity: see journal)\tThe railway tunnel is directly west of Gufi's camp, and can be reached by following the track directly there. Gufi has asked you to scout the tunnel into which the rails proceed.\n2\tPost signs at the dead ends (total: 3)\tSignposts can be found in the rail-tunnels of the Silvertine Lodes near the dead ends. You should hang signs where the rails lead to dead ends.\n3\tReturn to Gufi\tGufi is at the central encampment in the Silvertine Lodes. You should return to Gufi with the results of your survey.\n",
[2491]="70000D8D\n1\tTalk to Onar\tThe dwarf-merchant Onar is in the hamlet of Needlehole in the north-west corner of Rushock Bog. Hyacinth only needs brimstone and iron filings to get to work on Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' fireworks. She suggested you could obtain them from Onar, a dwarf-merchant.\n2\tBring brimstone and iron filings to Hyacinth Took\tHyacinth Took is in Tuckborough, near the Great Smials. Hyacinth Took sent you to Needlehole to acquire brimstone and iron filings from the dwarf-merchant Onar. Onar made a quick and fair trade and has sent you back to Hyacinth with her parcels.\n3\tTalk to Lobelia Sackville-Baggins\tLobelia Sackville-Baggins is at her home at Bag End in Hobbiton. With your help, Hyacinth Took now has all she needs to begin work on Lobelia Sackville-Baggins' fireworks. She told you to return to Lobelia and let her know the fireworks will be done in three months.\n",
[2492]="70037C85\n1\tDisable Siege Ladders ([see journal]/10)\030Defeat Trolls (total: 3)\tSaruman's army has constructed a large ladder with the ability to latch itself to the wall, making it difficult to detach. Destroy the hooks on the ladders and render them useless, and defeat the war trolls as they ascend to launch their assault. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2493]="700215CE\n1\tPresent the amulet to the mournful shade\030Present the amulet to the sorrowful shade\tThe sorrowful and mournful shades can be found to the north-west of the Hall of Sanctuary, near the entrances of several barrows on the ridge above. Lhudd has asked you to present the shades with the broken amulet that you recovered and observe what unfolds.\n2\tTalk to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary\tLhudd is at the Hall of Sanctuary, south-east of the barrows. You should return to Lhudd and explain the happenings outside of the barrows.\n",
[2494]="70028259\n1\tTalk to Naeglanc at Echad Naeglanc in the Bonevales\tNaeglanc is at Echad Naeglanc, south and west of Ilar's camp. Ilar told you to bring word of your discoveries to Naeglanc.\n",
[2495]="700272C5\n1\tTalk to Léofward at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tLéofward is at the Rohirrim scout-camp in the Gravenwood. Saeradan instructed you to speak with Léofward before continuing your journey southward.\n2\tTalk to Ardwyn in the Isendale\tArdwyn is at Forthbrond in the Isendale, south of the Gravenwood. Léofward asked you to take a report to Ardwyn regarding the strength of the Dunlending forces.\n",
[2496]="7000B3E1\n1\tPlace the Thistledown haunches on the flat stone in the Isendeep\030Collect Thistledown Haunches (total: 10)\tSearch the areas south of Tol Ascarnen or west along the plains, south of Dâr-gazag for the Thistledown Grazers. Collect some of their haunches and bring them to the slab within the depths of the Isendeep. Sergeant-at-Arms Thorfinn believes that the drakes can be used against the Orcs of Angmar and wishes to use them as a diversion while you attack the Tyrant.\n",
})
